 t('<b>Functions</b>', '<b>Formulate:</b> principal channel between grassroots and top decision-makers; give ministers facts and figures, court judgments, laws; technical considerations; <b>policy advice incl. value judgments</b>; draft legislation; help shape balanced policy for overall welfare, not just some sections', '<b>Implement</b> (a principal responsibility): making rules, financial management, HR management, regular monitoring and supervision', '<b>Evaluate:</b> feedback goes to political leadership to improve, adjust or modify policy, but a <span class="rd">conflict of interest</span> arises (officers evaluate programmes they implemented) → rising importance of <b>social audits</b>', '<b>Adjudicate:</b> quasi-judicial powers (e.g. District Collectors decide certain administrative disputes through revenue courts)', '<b>Continuity:</b> administration continues through changes in political leadership or absence of the political executive', w=22),
